Verdict: NEED_MORE
Rationale: The claim contains multiple material parts: (1) the Río Grande de Santiago River dam was completed in 2012, (2) it was inaugurated by Felipe de Jesús Calderón Hinojosa, and (3) he was the President of the country from 2006-2012. While one finding correctly identifies Felipe Calderón as the President of Mexico during 2006-2012 and a politician, it does not confirm that he inaugurated the dam. Additionally, no evidence confirms the completion year of the dam or its inauguration by Calderón. Therefore, the evidence is insufficient to support the full claim, and further investigation is needed.
